BT /F1 10 Tf 28 666.6 Td (1. What is the term for the grid structure organizing data into rows of cases and columns of attributes?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 653.6 Td (Answer: Data matrix \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 634.6 Td (2. What type of study observes without interfering and can only establish association?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 621.6 Td (Answer: Observational study \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 602.6 Td (3. What sampling bias occurs when only those with strong opinions opt in to participate?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 589.6 Td (Answer: Voluntary response bias \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 570.6 Td (4. What is the process of randomly assigning subjects to treatments to balance out other variables?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 557.6 Td (Answer: Randomization \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 538.6 Td (5. What do you call improvement that occurs simply because subjects believe they got a special treatment?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 525.6 Td (Answer: Placebo effect \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 506.6 Td (6. What type of variable has levels with a natural, inherent order?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 493.6 Td (Answer: Ordinal \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 474.6 Td (7. What sampling method divides the population into varied clusters, picks a few randomly, then samples everyone) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 461.6 Td (inside?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 448.6 Td (Answer: Cluster sampling \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 429.6 Td (8. What principle of experimental design involves comparing the treatment against a control group?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 416.6 Td (Answer: Control \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 397.6 Td (9. What is a survey of every individual in the entire population called?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 384.6 Td (Answer: Census \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 365.6 Td (10. What is the variable in an experiment that researchers impose as a condition being tested?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 352.6 Td (Answer: Explanatory variable \227 Correct) Tj ET
